e clips. IdleScreen gains a `data-testid='manage-clips-link'` button when `onOpenPair`-style `onOpenClips` prop is wired. App.tsx routes `view='clips'` through a `<Suspense>` boundary matching the PairScreen idiom. Verify-script `app/verify-phase6-1.mjs` runs C1–C4 gate-grade checks (Manage clips link present, library screen opens with empty state + close button + import label, quota-text DOM element renders, Close returns to IdleScreen). All four PASS with 0 console errors. M1–M7 manual checklist enumerates real-device QA per QUALITY_GATES.md §B5 (real <video> duration extraction + live navigator.storage math + .mp4-only acceptance + 200 MB cap + 100 MB soft warn). 23 new vitest tests (213 total, was 190; +2 db v3→v4 upgrade, +21 library across addClip/listClips/deleteClip/getQuotaEstimate/quotaBanner/isSoftWarnSize). Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Main bundle 346.49 KB / 107.15 KB gzip (Phase 2b.4 baseline 345.86 / 107.01 — delta +0.63 KB raw / +0.14 KB gzip thanks to lazy-loading; clip-library chunk separated). CSS chunk grew +1.06 KB raw / +0.21 KB gzip for `.clip-library*` styles. Budget was +5 KB gzip total → well under. Code-reviewer (`code-reviewer` agent) returned APPROVE with 0 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits; all five should-fixes applied before this approval (S1 lazy-load via React.lazy matching PairScreen pattern; S2 metadata extraction moved to `clipmode/metadata.ts`; S3 plain-object branch in `isQuotaError` removed since DOMException-only is what's tested + required; S4 URL.createObjectURL wrapped in try/catch returning 0 on throw; S5 verify-script C3 promoted from best-effort to gate check since headless chromium uniformly ships navigator.storage.estimate). Three of four nits applied: N1 dropped 'video/quicktime' to align with PHASES.md mp4-only criterion; N2 wired aria-disabled on the import label so the dead CSS rule now matches; N3 `fetchLibraryState()` helper deduplicates the effect/refresh data-fetch. Nit N4 (use a shared `rngId` helper) skipped — grepped and no such helper exists; `mintClipId` matches the existing pattern in `session.ts:81` and `profiles.ts:18` (each module mints its own `${prefix}-${Date.now()}-${rand}` id). docs/PHASES.md + docs/QUALITY_GATES.md were already updated in the prior Phase-6-decomposition iteration; this iteration touched only code + tests + verify script + results.",
